      "source": [
        "## **5. Loops**\n",
        "\n",
        "Loops let you repeat actions efficiently. Use a for loop when you need to iterate over a sequence or a known range of values. Use a while loop when repetition should continue while a condition holds true. Both loop types can be controlled using break and continue to exit early or skip iterations.\n",
        "\n",
        "When using loops, consider the termination condition carefully to avoid infinite loops. Also, prefer concise loop constructs and use list comprehensions when appropriate for simple transformations."
      ]
    },
