      "source": [
        "## **10. Functions**\n",
        "Functions encapsulate a sequence of statements to perform a specific task. They improve code reuse and readability by allowing you to call the same logic with different inputs. Define functions with def, specify parameters for inputs, and use return to provide results back to the caller.\n",
        "\n",
        "Good function design means keeping functions small and focused, using clear parameter names, and avoiding side effects when possible. This makes testing and maintenance easier."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "eba5aebb",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eba5aebb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **10.1 Why functions are useful**\n",
        "\n",
        "Functions group code to reuse and to improve readability."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "39e230d1",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "39e230d1"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def greet(name):\n",
        "    print('Hello', name)\n",
        "\n",
        "greet('Tom')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "db786e1b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "db786e1b"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Practice:** Write a function that prints 'Hello' and a name."
