      "source": [
        "## **11. File Handling**\n",
        "\n",
        "File handling allows programs to read from and write to files on disk, enabling persistent storage of data. Using the with open(...) as f: pattern ensures files are closed automatically, even if errors occur. Common methods include read(), readline(), readlines(), and write().\n",
        "\n",
        "When writing files, consider encoding and newline behavior for portability. For small datasets, text files are sufficient; for structured data prefer formats like CSV or JSON with the appropriate libraries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ce9f46a8",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ce9f46a8"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **11.1 Opening files (open())**\n",
        "\n",
        "Use open(filename, mode) to access files: 'r' read, 'w' write, 'a' append."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "63958e85",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "63958e85"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# create a sample file\n",
        "with open('sample.txt', 'w') as f:\n",
        "    f.write('line1\\nline2')\n",
        "\n",
        "f = open('sample.txt', 'r')\n",
        "print(f.read())\n",
        "f.close()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f6fb1076",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f6fb1076"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Practice:** Open a file for writing, write 2 lines, then read it back."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XLz7J_5HCr9T"
      },
      "id": "XLz7J_5HCr9T",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2ffa8fb6",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2ffa8fb6"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **11.2 Reading files (read, readline, readlines)**\n",
        "\n",
        "read() reads all, readline() reads one line, readlines() returns list of lines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "778099b4",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "778099b4"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "with open('sample.txt', 'r') as f:\n",
        "    print('read():')\n",
        "    print(f.read())\n",
        "\n",
        "with open('sample.txt', 'r') as f:\n",
        "    print('readline():')\n",
        "    print(f.readline())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b55b2bc0",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b55b2bc0"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Practice:** Use readlines() to get a list of lines and print its length."
      ]
