      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e6cbe9c9",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e6cbe9c9"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **11.3 Writing to files (write, writelines)**\n",
        "\n",
        "Use write() to add text; writelines() writes a list of strings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "1a5ff50c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1a5ff50c"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "with open('out.txt', 'w') as f:\n",
        "    f.write('Hello\\n')\n",
        "    f.writelines(['A\\n','B\\n'])\n",
        "with open('out.txt') as f:\n",
        "    print(f.read())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "404310a8",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "404310a8"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Practice:** Write three lines to a file and read them."
